    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick\n\n### Question\n\nI saw this example in the help file:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n-- Adding custom picker to pick `register` entries\r\nMiniPick.registry.registry = function()\r\n  local items = vim.tbl_keys(MiniPick.registry)\r\n  table.sort(items)\r\n  local source = {items = items, name = 'Registry', choose = function() end}\r\n  local chosen_picker_name = MiniPick.start({ source = source })\r\n  if chosen_picker_name == nil then return end\r\n  return MiniPick.registry[chosen_picker_name]()\r\nend\r\n```\r\n\r\nI'm wondering why it wasn't just written like this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nMiniPick.registry.registry = function()\r\n  local items = vim.tbl_keys(MiniPick.registry)\r\n  table.sort(items)\r\n  MiniPick.start({\r\n    source = {\r\n      items = items,\r\n      name = \"Registry\",\r\n      choose = function(item)\r\n        if item == nil then return end\r\n        MiniPick.registry[item]()\r\n      end,\r\n    },\r\n  })\r\nend\r\n```\r\n",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.pick</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I saw this example in the help file:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"-- Adding custom picker to pick `register` entries\nMiniPick.registry.registry = function()\n  local items = vim.tbl_keys(MiniPick.registry)\n  table.sort(items)\n  local source = {items = items, name = 'Registry', choose = function() end}\n  local chosen_picker_name = MiniPick.start({ source = source })\n  if chosen_picker_name == nil then return end\n  return MiniPick.registry[chosen_picker_name]()\nend\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> Adding custom picker to pick `register` entries</span>\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniPick</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">registry</span>.<span class=\"pl-en\">registry</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>()\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">items</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">tbl_keys</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniPick</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">registry</span>)\n  <span class=\"pl-c1\">table.sort</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">items</span>)\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">source</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {<span class=\"pl-smi\">items</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">items</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">name</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>Registry<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-en\">choose</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>() <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>}\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">chosen_picker_name</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniPick</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">start</span>({ <span class=\"pl-smi\">source</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">source</span> })\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">if</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">chosen_picker_name</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">==</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">nil</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">then</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniPick</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">registry</span>[<span class=\"pl-smi\">chosen_picker_name</span>]()\n<span class=\"pl-k\">end</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I'm wondering why it wasn't just written like this:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"MiniPick.registry.registry = function()\n  local items = vim.tbl_keys(MiniPick.registry)\n  table.sort(items)\n  MiniPick.start({\n    source = {\n      items = items,\n      name = &quot;Registry&quot;,\n      choose = function(item)\n        if item == nil then return end\n        MiniPick.registry[item]()\n      end,\n    },\n  })\nend\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniPick</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">registry</span>.<span class=\"pl-en\">registry</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>()\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">items</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">tbl_keys</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniPick</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">registry</span>)\n  <span class=\"pl-c1\">table.sort</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">items</span>)\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniPick</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">start</span>({\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">source</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n      <span class=\"pl-smi\">items</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">items</span>,\n      <span class=\"pl-smi\">name</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>Registry<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>,\n      <span class=\"pl-en\">choose</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">item</span>)\n        <span class=\"pl-k\">if</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">item</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">==</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">nil</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">then</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n        <span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniPick</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">registry</span>[<span class=\"pl-smi\">item</span>]()\n      <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>,\n    },\n  })\n<span class=\"pl-k\">end</span></pre></div>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.pick\nQuestion\nI saw this example in the help file:\n-- Adding custom picker to pick `register` entries\nMiniPick.registry.registry = function()\n  local items = vim.tbl_keys(MiniPick.registry)\n  table.sort(items)\n  local source = {items = items, name = 'Registry', choose = function() end}\n  local chosen_picker_name = MiniPick.start({ source = source })\n  if chosen_picker_name == nil then return end\n  return MiniPick.registry[chosen_picker_name]()\nend\nI'm wondering why it wasn't just written like this:\nMiniPick.registry.registry = function()\n  local items = vim.tbl_keys(MiniPick.registry)\n  table.sort(items)\n  MiniPick.start({\n    source = {\n      items = items,\n      name = \"Registry\",\n      choose = function(item)\n        if item == nil then return end\n        MiniPick.registry[item]()\n      end,\n    },\n  })\nend",
